  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "The Fedora development team will focus on providing a",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "message-oriented middleware solution for the Fedora",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "Service Framework that will be based on an open-source",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "implementation of the Java Message Service (JMS) API. ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "This will entail JMS-enabling the core Fedora",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "repository so that it can publish messages (e.g., API",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "events). Also a JMS message broker will be",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "implemented in the framework to facilitate",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "publish/subscribe of messages between the Fedora",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "repository and other services (i.e.,",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "preservation-oriented services, and other services).",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
